  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VACS - Vision for Adapted Crops and Soils</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Vision for Adapted Crops and Soils (VACS) initiative aims to address food security and nutrition challenges in Africa by revitalizing indigenous and traditional food crops. Currently, one in five people in Africa face chronic hunger, and this number could rise to 310 million by 2030 due to climate change. VACS aims to build resilient agrifood systems by focusing on soil health and crop selection. VACS is being implemented in three phases:

- Phase 1 (completed in May 2023) aimed to identify the most important crops for nutrition in Africa through a consultative process involving experts primarily based on the African continent.

- Phase 2 (ongoing) will assess how these crops will fare under climate change through the year 2050 across five sub-regions of Africa.

- Phase 3 (ongoing) will seek to mobilize resources to accelerate research, development, and deployment of these crops. This phase aims to deliver high-yielding, locally adapted varieties to farmers and consumers to improve food security and nutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
